-- ============================================================
-- Alonecraft 4.61 -- Rogue / Subtlety
--   Hemorrhage -> no charges, and the debuff scales with attack power
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md:
--   "Hemorrhage: Physical damage increase no longer has charges and is
--    increased by attack power."
--
--
-- 16511 / 17347 / 17348 / 26864 / 48660
--
--   Hemorrhage's debuff is its own effect 3: MOD_DAMAGE_TAKEN (14) with
--   EffectMiscValue 1 (physical), a flat 13/21/29/42/75 added to every
--   physical hit the target takes, limited to 10 charges over 15 s.
--
--   ProcCharges 10 -> 0 removes the charge limit; the 15 s duration is now
--   the only limit, which is a real buff -- at 5 ranks the debuff went from
--   at most 10 hits to every hit for the full window.
--
--   The attack power half cannot be expressed in the DBC (there is no
--   coefficient field for MOD_DAMAGE_TAKEN), so the flat amount is topped
--   up in spell_rog_hemorrhage (RogueHemorrhage.cpp) from the rogue's
--   melee attack power at the moment the debuff is applied.
--
--   TUNING: the coefficient is 5% of attack power, i.e. about +200 per hit
--   at 4000 AP against a rank-5 base of 75.  That is deliberately generous
--   in the Alonecraft "talents should matter" direction and is the single
--   number here most likely to need retuning after play.  It lives in
--   HEMORRHAGE_AP_PCT in RogueHemorrhage.cpp.
--
--   Only the descriptions change besides ProcCharges -- the old text
--   promised "$n charges", which is no longer true.
--
-- ============================================================


